            <ArticleTitle>[ENT considerations of head and facial pain (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>397-402</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To the otolaryngologist, there are multiple causes for head or facial pain: headaches due to ear diseases; idiopathic neuralgias; &quot;referred otalgia&quot; involving cranial nerves V, IX, X; temporomandibular joint dysfunction; rhinological pathologies, including post-traumatic trigeminal neuralgia; &quot;facial sympathalgias&quot;; the styloid process syndrome; and cervical spine problems. Less known causes of head and neck pain are stressed, and emphasis placed on their diagnosis and treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
